From 0d888603f256b6f0819e46d4c641e1c626d5be5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 08:02:12 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] libply-splash-core: Let a theme draw both eyes of a
 stereo output

A theme that declares Stereo=full-side-by-side in its [Plymouth Theme]
group draws both eyes at full size side by side, the left eye in the
left half. The splash asks each pixel display for that; a renderer that
can show it makes the display twice an eye's width, and every other
display stays one picture, drawn once. Themes without the key are
unchanged: a stereo output gives their one picture to both eyes.

The script plugin gets Window.GetStereo (), true when the window holds
both eyes, so a theme can lay itself out for one picture or two.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code
